{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1708340,
  "courseSlug": "learn-flutter-dart-to-build-ios-android-apps",
  "courseTitle": "Flutter & Dart - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "37130562",
      "title": "Adding Buttons & Using Functions As Values",
      "lectureOrder": 46,
      "videoOrder": 43,
      "sourceHash": "c3fb5188622be8183975060331feb5d51e526904a78dcbc29efbb064d0187f1c",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.1,
          "end": 4.86,
          "en": "Now, having this dice image here is nice,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.86,
          "end": 8.19,
          "en": "but we, of course, also want to have a button below that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.19,
          "end": 11.283,
          "en": "which can be pressed to roll the dice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.12,
          "end": 14.34,
          "en": "And therefore, we should, of course, add such a button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.34,
          "end": 16.53,
          "en": "To do that, it's no longer enough",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.53,
          "end": 20.55,
          "en": "to just have a single child in this Center widget,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.55,
          "end": 22.893,
          "en": "but instead, we need multiple widgets here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.97,
          "end": 27.81,
          "en": "Now, Center only has this child argument, though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.81,
          "end": 29.7,
          "en": "I mean, it has other arguments as well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.7,
          "end": 32.31,
          "en": "but those don't take any widgets at all.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.31,
          "end": 34.65,
          "en": "So it only takes one single widget.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.65,
          "end": 35.91,
          "en": "So what can we do now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.91,
          "end": 38.52,
          "en": "if we actually wanna provide multiple widgets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.52,
          "end": 40.44,
          "en": "as child widgets here?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.44,
          "end": 44.97,
          "en": "Well, we need another widget in between the Column widget,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.97,
          "end": 46.74,
          "en": "which is another key widget",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.74,
          "end": 50.46,
          "en": "that you will be using a lot when working with Flutter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.46,
          "end": 52.17,
          "en": "The column widget exists",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 52.17,
          "end": 55.59,
          "en": "to allow you to render multiple widgets,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 55.59,
          "end": 59.07,
          "en": "multiple children above each other.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 59.07,
          "end": 61.17,
          "en": "There also is a row widget,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 61.17,
          "end": 65.43,
          "en": "which would do the same but next to each other horizontally.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 65.43,
          "end": 68.49,
          "en": "Here I want to have widgets above each other vertically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 68.49,
          "end": 70.59,
          "en": "and therefore, Column is the right choice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 71.78999999999999,
          "end": 74.25,
          "en": "Now, the children argument, which can be set here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 74.25,
          "end": 76.05,
          "en": "then takes a list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 76.05,
          "end": 79.08,
          "en": "So we need opening and closing square brackets,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 79.08,
          "end": 81.423,
          "en": "and it takes a list of widgets.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 82.86,
          "end": 86.43,
          "en": "So therefore, here, we can now take our image",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 86.43,
          "end": 89.37,
          "en": "and move that into that list here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 89.37,
          "end": 93.09,
          "en": "And then below that image, we can display our button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 93.09,
          "end": 96.69,
          "en": "Now, of course, buttons are a very common type of widget,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 96.69,
          "end": 100.89,
          "en": "and indeed, Flutter supports three different main buttons.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 100.89,
          "end": 105.39,
          "en": "It has the ElevatedButton here for displaying a button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 105.39,
          "end": 108.99000000000001,
          "en": "that has a background color and a slight shadow.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 108.99000000000001,
          "end": 112.59,
          "en": "It has the OutlinedButton for displaying a button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 112.59,
          "end": 115.86,
          "en": "that has no background color, but a border.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 115.86,
          "end": 119.19,
          "en": "And it has the TextButton for displaying a button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 119.19,
          "end": 121.32,
          "en": "that is only some pressable text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 121.32,
          "end": 124.32,
          "en": "And that's the kind of button I want to display here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 124.32,
          "end": 126.12,
          "en": "though, of course, you can play around",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 126.12,
          "end": 129.15,
          "en": "with that and also give other buttons a try.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 129.15,
          "end": 131.52,
          "en": "Now, when I use autocompletion here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 131.52,
          "end": 134.46,
          "en": "so when I hit Tab after selecting TextButton,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 134.46,
          "end": 138,
          "en": "I automatically get two named arguments added here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 138,
          "end": 139.833,
          "en": "child and onPressed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 141.15,
          "end": 143.4,
          "en": "Now, child is the simpler one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 143.4,
          "end": 145.82999999999998,
          "en": "Child simply wants another widget,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 145.82999999999998,
          "end": 148.53,
          "en": "which is wrapped inside of that button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 148.53,
          "end": 150.66,
          "en": "And typically, that's a Text widget",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 150.66,
          "end": 152.61,
          "en": "which holds the text that should be shown",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 152.61,
          "end": 154.98,
          "en": "on the button, because, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 154.98,
          "end": 156.84,
          "en": "this TextButton should show some text;",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 156.84,
          "end": 158.69,
          "en": "otherwise, you wouldn't see anything.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 159.57,
          "end": 163.2,
          "en": "So here, this could, for example, be Roll Dice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 163.2,
          "end": 164.73,
          "en": "Now, I get some blue squiggly lines here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 164.73,
          "end": 166.56,
          "en": "because here we can add const",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 166.56,
          "end": 168.873,
          "en": "to allow for some optional caching.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 169.95,
          "end": 172.773,
          "en": "But what is this onPressed argument all about now?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 173.7,
          "end": 178.7,
          "en": "Well, onPressed actually wants a function or null",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 179.13,
          "end": 182.55,
          "en": "as a value, and that is something new.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 182.55,
          "end": 183.99,
          "en": "Up to this point, we worked",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 183.99,
          "end": 188.22,
          "en": "with a lot of different values; with text, with numbers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 188.22,
          "end": 191.1,
          "en": "but also of course, with many objects and widgets,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 191.1,
          "end": 194.76,
          "en": "but we never used functions as values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 194.76,
          "end": 196.47,
          "en": "but you can do that in Dart.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 196.47,
          "end": 200.82,
          "en": "Functions in Dart are also just objects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 200.82,
          "end": 202.32,
          "en": "So if you define a function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 202.32,
          "end": 205.29,
          "en": "you can pass a function as a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 205.29,
          "end": 208.02,
          "en": "to arguments that want a function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 208.02,
          "end": 211.2,
          "en": "And here for onPressed, you have two main options.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 211.2,
          "end": 215.49,
          "en": "Option 1 is that you define the function just in place.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 215.49,
          "end": 217.65,
          "en": "This is done like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 217.65,
          "end": 219.72,
          "en": "by adding opening and closing parentheses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 219.72,
          "end": 222.394,
          "en": "and then opening and closing curly braces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 222.394,
          "end": 225.87,
          "en": "This is a so-called anonymous function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 225.87,
          "end": 230.13,
          "en": "It doesn't have a name like clickHandler",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 230.13,
          "end": 233.64,
          "en": "or anything like that, and it doesn't want a name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 233.64,
          "end": 235.17000000000002,
          "en": "Instead, this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 235.17000000000002,
          "end": 237.54,
          "en": "is defined here in this place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 237.54,
          "end": 239.46,
          "en": "where a function is needed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 239.46,
          "end": 243.3,
          "en": "so that it's provided as a value to onPressed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 243.3,
          "end": 245.76,
          "en": "This function is then executed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 245.76,
          "end": 248.76,
          "en": "called internally by TextButton",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 248.76,
          "end": 251.553,
          "en": "when it registers a click on the button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 252.51,
          "end": 254.28,
          "en": "So this function is only used here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 254.28,
          "end": 255.78,
          "en": "can't be used anywhere else,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 255.78,
          "end": 257.82,
          "en": "and that's why it doesn't have a name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 257.82,
          "end": 259.32,
          "en": "But between those curly braces,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 259.32,
          "end": 261.27,
          "en": "you can define any code you want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 261.27,
          "end": 264.21,
          "en": "that should be executed when this function is called.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 264.21,
          "end": 266.85,
          "en": "So when this button is pressed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 266.85,
          "end": 267.993,
          "en": "That's Option 1.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 269.04,
          "end": 273.9,
          "en": "Option 2 is that you define a method, for example, here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 273.9,
          "end": 277.38,
          "en": "after all our constructors and these variables,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 277.38,
          "end": 280.413,
          "en": "and that could be a method called rollDice,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 282.46500000000003,
          "end": 283.71,
          "en": "as you always did,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 283.71,
          "end": 287.43,
          "en": "by providing a name and then also a return value, which,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 287.43,
          "end": 288.96,
          "en": "in this case, should be void,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 288.96,
          "end": 293.96,
          "en": "because onPressed wants a function that returns nothing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 294.45,
          "end": 296.28,
          "en": "So therefore, here, you should have void,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 296.28,
          "end": 297.69,
          "en": "then your function name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 297.69,
          "end": 301.08,
          "en": "and then here, whatever code you want to execute.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 301.08,
          "end": 303.9,
          "en": "And now you can use that function name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 303.9,
          "end": 307.14,
          "en": "and use that as a argument value here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 307.14,
          "end": 309.51,
          "en": "So you don't execute the function here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 309.51,
          "end": 311.28,
          "en": "you don't add parentheses,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 311.28,
          "end": 313.23,
          "en": "you just use the function name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 313.23,
          "end": 316.86,
          "en": "to basically pass a pointer to that function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 316.86,
          "end": 318.753,
          "en": "as a value to onPressed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 319.98,
          "end": 323.61,
          "en": "With that, onPressed knows where to find this function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 323.61,
          "end": 325.41,
          "en": "and internally, TextButton",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 325.41,
          "end": 329.637,
          "en": "will execute that function here when the button is pressed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 329.637,
          "end": 333.39,
          "en": "Now, I personally typically prefer this approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 333.39,
          "end": 336.12,
          "en": "of having a separate function that's then passed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 336.12,
          "end": 339.65999999999997,
          "en": "as a pointer, so to say, by using the function name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 339.65999999999997,
          "end": 343.14,
          "en": "But you could also use this anonymous function instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 343.14,
          "end": 345.68,
          "en": "But here, I'll go for the separate function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 345.68,
          "end": 347.76,
          "en": "And now here inside of Roll Dice,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 347.76,
          "end": 349.47,
          "en": "we can do whatever we want to do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 349.47,
          "end": 351.51,
          "en": "when this button is pressed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 351.51,
          "end": 354.12,
          "en": "If we save everything and reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 354.12,
          "end": 355.83,
          "en": "we now see this button here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 355.83,
          "end": 356.88,
          "en": "It looks a bit strange.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 356.88,
          "end": 359.88,
          "en": "It's at the top and the button styling isn't final,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 359.88,
          "end": 362.94,
          "en": "but as you can see, it can be clicked.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 362.94,
          "end": 364.89,
          "en": "Now it's time to fix the styling",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 364.89,
          "end": 367.353,
          "en": "and then do something when the button is clicked.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
